# Kafka on __CLUSTER_NAME__

Workload: Apache Kafka in KRaft mode (no ZooKeeper)
Brokers: __BROKERS__
Storage per broker: __STORAGE_SIZE__
DB nodes: __DB_NODE_COUNT__
Region: __REGION__

## Bootstrap addresses

**Internal** (in-cluster pods, e.g. Cassandra sidecar):
```
kafka.default.svc.cluster.local:9092
```

**External** (from outside the cluster via Tailscale):
```
__CONTROL_HOST_PRIVATE__:32100
```

## Metrics

The OTel collector scrapes the broker JMX exporters (`job="kafka-jmx"`) and the Kafka Exporter
(`job="kafka-exporter"`) directly on each pod's port 9404, by pod discovery. Query them in
Grafana; see `METRICS.md` for the metric names.

The same endpoints stay exposed on NodePorts for manual inspection:

```bash
curl http://__CONTROL_HOST_PRIVATE__:32404/metrics   # broker JMX exporter
curl http://__CONTROL_HOST_PRIVATE__:32309/metrics   # Kafka Exporter
```

## Use cases

### CDC: Cassandra → Kafka → OpenSearch

Configure the Cassandra sidecar CDC connector with bootstrap server:
```
kafka.default.svc.cluster.local:9092
```

The internal address avoids NodePort overhead for pod-to-pod traffic.

### Kafka benchmarking

Produce and consume from outside the cluster using the external bootstrap:
```
__CONTROL_HOST_PRIVATE__:32100
```

Example with kafka-producer-perf-test:
```bash
kafka-producer-perf-test.sh \
  --topic test \
  --num-records 1000000 \
  --record-size 1024 \
  --throughput -1 \
  --producer-props bootstrap.servers=__CONTROL_HOST_PRIVATE__:32100
```

## Topic management

```bash
easy-db-lab kafka create-topic --topic my-topic --partitions 3 --replication-factor 1
```
